+# Pilot Conversion Email Templates
+
+These templates are for manual, human-reviewed outreach only. They do not claim guaranteed tender wins, automated bid submission, or traction that has not been evidenced.
+
+## 1. Pilot Invitation Email
+
+Subject: 2-week tender intelligence pilot for your bid team
+
+Hi {{first_name}},
+
+I am running a small 2-week validation pilot for ProcessEd, a tender intelligence dashboard for construction, civils, infrastructure, and public-sector bid teams.
+
+The live demo is a Hostinger static dashboard using TenderNed JSON metadata. It currently shows 50 Dutch tenders, 21 shortlisted opportunities, 45 tracked buyers, 5 hot outreach items, and 7 timing-ready opportunities.
+
+The pilot is simple: we review the dashboard against your target sectors and regions, track useful buyers, and send a short weekly summary of the opportunities worth looking at.
+
+It is not automated bid submission, legal/procurement advice, or a guarantee of tender wins. The VPS production pipeline is still unverified, and UK production ingestion is not part of this pilot unless verified later.
+
+Would a 20-minute walkthrough be useful next week?
+
+Best,
+Bilal
+
+## 2. Post-Demo Follow-Up
+
+Subject: ProcessEd pilot next steps
+
+Hi {{first_name}},
+
+Thanks for taking a look at the ProcessEd dashboard.
+
+Based on the demo, the sensible pilot would be:
+
+- confirm your target work types and exclusion rules
+- review shortlisted opportunities from the live Hostinger dashboard
+- track relevant buyers and timing-ready opportunities
+- send one concise weekly summary
+- review after two weeks whether the signal is strong enough to continue
+
+The current demo uses TenderNed JSON metadata. The Hostinger static dashboard is live; the VPS production pipeline remains unverified.
+
+If useful, I can set up a lightweight pilot tracker and start with one sector/region focus.
+
+Best,
+Bilal
+
+## 3. Mid-Pilot Check-In
+
+Subject: Quick pilot check-in
+
+Hi {{first_name}},
+
+Quick check-in on the ProcessEd pilot.
+
+Could you score the latest shortlist against three things?
+
+- Relevance: were the opportunities close enough to your target work?
+- Timing: did any items deserve review sooner than you would normally catch them?
+- Buyer insight: were any buyers worth tracking or researching further?
+
+No need for a long response. A few comments on what to include, exclude, or reweight will help tune the next summary.
+
+Best,
+Bilal
+
+## 4. End-Of-Pilot Conversion Email
+
+Subject: ProcessEd pilot review
+
+Hi {{first_name}},
+
+We have reached the end of the 2-week ProcessEd validation pilot.
+
+The decision point is whether the dashboard and weekly summary created enough value to justify continuing as a paid intelligence workflow.
+
+The main things to review are:
+
+- how many shortlisted tenders were genuinely relevant
+- whether the dashboard saved manual scanning time
+- whether buyer tracking was useful
+- whether timing-ready opportunities changed follow-up priority
+- what would need to be added before this becomes part of your weekly process
+
+If the signal is strong, I suggest we agree a narrow paid continuation around one sector, one region, and a weekly review pack. If it is not strong enough yet, I will capture the gaps and close the pilot cleanly.
+
+Best,
+Bilal
+
+## 5. Soft No-Response Follow-Up
+
+Subject: Close the loop?
+
+Hi {{first_name}},
+
+Just closing the loop on the ProcessEd pilot idea.
+
+The current demo is best suited to teams that want faster tender triage, buyer tracking, and timing signals from public-sector opportunity data. If that is not a priority right now, no problem.
+
+Should I leave this for now, or would it still be useful to send a short example dashboard summary?
+
+Best,
+Bilal
+
